# LongRoad.Core & LongRoad

## Core

- Bridge Domain to Unity: persistence, clocks, asset loading facades, service locators/DI.
- May use Unity APIs; must not contain Oregon Trail rules that belong in Domain.
- Reference Domain types; do not let presentation details leak into Domain interfaces.

## LongRoad (presentation)

- MonoBehaviours, UI Toolkit/uGUI, Input System wiring, scene lifecycle.
- Call into Domain/Core; avoid duplicating game rules in Update/UI callbacks.
- Keep components thin: read state, send intents/commands, render results.

## Both

- Root namespaces: `LongRoad.Core` / `LongRoad`.
- Do not reference Editor-only APIs from runtime assemblies.
- Prefer composing Domain use-cases over embedding logic in Inspector-serialized fields.
